schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Legal Wrapper
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A registered entity (co-op, nonprofit, LLC, or DAO-specific structure)
    that sits "around" a community group so the entity, not individual
    members, holds money, signs contracts, and absorbs liability.
  source_traditions:
    - traditional corporate/nonprofit/cooperative law
    - emerging DAO-specific legal-personality statutes (Wyoming DUNA, DAO LLC)
    - default general-partnership liability law (the "do-nothing" baseline)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Framed as risk-matched, not aspiration-matched — "match the structure to
    the risk, not to how serious you want to look," with a five-step
    decision path from "stay informal" to "Wyoming DUNA" to "offshore, only
    for large cross-border treasuries."
  adjacent_meanings:
    - unincorporated association (the default, zero-protection starting state)
    - fiscal sponsorship/fiscal host (a lighter-weight alternative that defers full incorporation)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      Legal Wrapper ≠ DAO — a DAO-specific wrapper (DUNA, DAO LLC) is one
      *kind* of legal wrapper suited to groups already voting on-chain or
      holding a multisig treasury; a co-op or nonprofit wrapper requires no
      on-chain governance at all
    - >-
      general partnership (default, unlimited personal liability) ≠ any
      registered wrapper (liability sits with the entity)
  tensions:
    - >-
      cost/complexity scales enormously across wrapper types — from "$0,
      stay informal" to Cayman Islands setup (~US$2,250 plus thousands/year
      in ongoing fees) — and the article explicitly warns against
      "over-wrapping," i.e. choosing based on aspiration rather than actual risk
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Presenting a single "decision path" checklist can read as more settled
    law than it is — DAO-specific wrappers (DUNA, DAO LLC) are recent
    (Wyoming DUNA effective July 2024) and largely untested in court; their
    liability-shield claims rest on statute and early adoption (e.g.
    Uniswap's DUNI), not extensive case law.
  maturity: raw
  public_use: requires-domain-review
  ai_assisted: true
  high_risk: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/legal-structures.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
